hxmc licenses
=============

This repository is a port of the Haxe compiler (https://github.com/HaxeFoundation/haxe)
and follows its licensing.

- The compiler port (haxe/src), the hxmc tool (hxmc/src, hxmc/bootstrap), the tests (haxe/test, hxmc/test), the npm packages' launcher (packages/) and the
  website (site/)
  are licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your
  option) any later version (SPDX: GPL-2.0-or-later). The full text is in COPYING.
  Copyright (C) 2005-2025 Haxe Foundation (the upstream compiler this is
  translated from), (c) 2026 the haxe-in-haxe contributors.

- Code that ends up in programs built with hxmc is licensed under the MIT License,
  so those programs are not bound by the GPL:
    hxmc/deps/ the scripts that build the runtime objects (hxmc/deps/LICENSE)
    hxmc/std/  the hxmc target's standard library and the runtime's
               Haxe part                              (hxmc/std/LICENSE)

- haxe/src/libs/ reproduces OCaml libraries that upstream Haxe depends on, under
  their own licenses:
    haxe/src/libs/neko/    from haxe/upstream/libs/neko (Neko compiler): GPL-2.0-or-later
    haxe/src/libs/swflib/  from haxe/upstream/libs/swflib: GPL-2.0
    haxe/src/libs/extlib/  from haxe/upstream/libs/extlib-leftovers (ExtLib): LGPL-2.1
                           with the OCaml linking exception
    haxe/src/libs/ziplib/  from haxe/upstream/libs/ziplib: LGPL-2.1 with the OCaml
                           linking exception
    haxe/src/libs/extc/    Zlib.hx is a translation of zlib 1.3.1's deflate
                           (Copyright (C) 1995-2024 Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler,
                           zlib license); Extc.hx follows haxe/upstream/libs/extc: GPL-2.0

- tools/lix/ is a port of lix.client and haxeshim (https://github.com/lix-pm), which are
  in the public domain (tools/lix/LICENSE, the Unlicense), and is released the same way.
  Its build includes hxcoro (https://github.com/HaxeFoundation/hxcoro), under its own
  license.

- The haxe/upstream submodule is upstream Haxe with its own LICENSE: the compiler is
  GPL-2.0-or-later and its standard library (haxe/upstream/std) MIT.

- site/playground/: some examples are from try.haxe.org (MIT,
  site/playground/LICENSE-try-haxe.txt).

- Programs built by hxmc that use sys.ssl or libuv (the port's release binaries
  and lix among them) link mbedtls (Apache-2.0) and libuv (MIT); their licenses
  ship with those binaries (LICENSE.mbedtls, LICENSE.libuv).
